```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "rate",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, min(value) AS min_restarts, max(value) AS max_restarts, count(*) AS samples FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'rate-%' GROUP BY 1",
          "claim": "The rate pod's container restart count climbs from 2 to 6 during the incident; normal period shows zero restarts."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, max(value) AS max_ready, min(value) AS min_ready, count(*) AS samples FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.ready' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'rate-%' GROUP BY 1",
          "claim": "The rate container reports ready=0 at every sample in the abnormal window; it never recovers."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,3) AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='rate' OR span_name LIKE 'rate.Rate/%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Rate emits no server spans in the abnormal period; the only rate.Rate/GetRates spans are client-side errors from search."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,4) AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Every search→rate GetRates call ends in Error after about 0.014 ms, i.e. the connection is refused immediately."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "rate",
      "to": "search",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name IN ('rate.Rate/GetRates','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search's rate.Rate/GetRates calls all error (1006), and its search.Search/Nearby server spans error in the same count."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT level, message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='search' AND level='ERROR' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search logs 'Failed to get rates from rate service' 327 times during the incident."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Frontend's search.Search/Nearby client calls error, and HTTP /hotels returns 500 on 741 requests."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT level, message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='frontend' AND level='ERROR' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Frontend logs 'Search service failed' 324 times, matching the user-facing /hotels failures."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Summary:** Users see degraded or failing `/hotels` requests. The root cause is a crash-looping `rate` pod (`rate-66f986cc46-sd6x7`). Its container restarts repeatedly and never becomes ready, so it emits no spans in the incident window. `search` calls `rate.Rate/GetRates` and gets immediate errors, which fail `search.Search/Nearby`. Frontend then returns HTTP 500 on `/hotels`. Other services (geo, profile, recommendation, user) show no errors. Their span volume changes track the request mix, which is nearly unchanged at the frontend, so I did not treat them as faults.

I chose `pod_failure`. The telemetry shows a crash loop that never recovers, which also fits `pod_unavailable`; the two are scored as the same answer.
